1
00:05:12,631 --> 00:05:18,631
He gave the West justice right up to its neck...
then rammed more down its throat.

2
00:10:25,263 --> 00:10:31,263
Lawman is a western film directed by Michael Winner.

3
00:15:37,894 --> 00:15:43,894
While passing through the town of Bannock, a bunch of drunken cattlemen go overboard
with their celebrating and accidentally kill an old man with a stray shot.

4
00:20:50,526 --> 00:20:56,526
They return home to Sabbath unaware of his death.

5
00:26:03,157 --> 00:26:09,157
Bannock lawman Jered Maddox later arrives there to arrest
everyone involved on a charge of murder.

6
00:31:15,789 --> 00:31:21,789
Sabbath is run by land baron Vince Bronson, a benevolent despot, who, upon
hearing of the death, offers restitution for the incident.

7
00:36:28,421 --> 00:36:34,421
Bannock Marshal Jared Maddox, played by Burt Lancaster.

8
00:41:41,052 --> 00:41:47,052
Sabbath Marshal Cotton Ryan, played by Robert Ryan.

9
00:46:53,684 --> 00:46:59,684
Vincent Bronson, played by Lee J. Cobb.

10
00:52:06,315 --> 00:52:12,315
Vernon Adams, played by Robert Duvall.

11
00:57:18,947 --> 00:57:24,947
Laura Shelby, played by Sheree North.

12
01:02:31,578 --> 01:02:37,578
Harvey Stenbaugh, played by Albert Salmi.

13
01:07:44,210 --> 01:07:50,210
Lawman is a 1971 American revisionist Western film produced and directed by
Michael Winner and starring Burt Lancaster, Robert Ryan, Lee J.

14
01:12:56,842 --> 01:13:02,842
Cobb, Sheree North, and Robert Duvall.

15
01:18:09,473 --> 01:18:15,473
The screenplay by Gerald Wilson focuses on Jered Maddox, a rigid marshal who arrives in a small town to arrest a group of cattlemen for the
accidental death of an old man, sparking a conflict between his absolute adherence to the law and the community's pragmatic desire for peace.

16
01:23:22,105 --> 01:23:28,105
Filmed on location in Durango, Mexico, Lawman was Winner's
first Western and his first American production.

17
01:28:34,736 --> 01:28:40,736
The film explores themes of justice, obsession, and the
changing nature of the American frontier.

18
01:33:47,368 --> 01:33:53,368
It received mixed reviews upon release but has since garnered
appreciation for its moral complexity and performances.
